WEBVTT

00:11.910 --> 00:17.830
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

01:30.440 --> 01:34.700
What's in there? What's in there?

01:38.830 --> 01:40.500
We're finally out!

01:40.500 --> 01:41.960
Akitsuakane too?!

01:44.080 --> 01:47.670
H-How did you two get delivered here?

01:48.170 --> 01:48.880
#43: THE SCARLET WHALE

01:48.880 --> 01:51.050
#43: THE SCARLET WHALE
What's going on here?

01:51.050 --> 01:53.180
AND THE MONSTER OF THE SEA

01:53.180 --> 01:56.760
I'm not really sure myself.

02:00.520 --> 02:02.270
When I was seeing the sea...

02:04.190 --> 02:06.020
What a beautiful sea!

02:06.020 --> 02:08.000
So many ships!

02:10.030 --> 02:11.150
UNIQUE SCENARIO

02:11.150 --> 02:14.030
PIERCE THE DISCIPLE OF THE ABYSS - BEGIN?
A message window suddenly popped out.

02:14.030 --> 02:18.620
What? Unique Scenario?
The thing Sunraku talked about?

02:18.620 --> 02:20.400
Why am I getting this?

02:28.170 --> 02:31.320
Make way, make way, make way,
make way, make way, make way!

02:35.340 --> 02:40.100
It's the Redwhale Pirates'
famous "Barrel Delivery"!

02:44.060 --> 02:45.100
Got them!

02:45.100 --> 02:48.090
What is happening?!

02:48.090 --> 02:52.570
They threw us into the barrel,
and the next thing I know we're here.

02:53.240 --> 02:55.280
That's way too scary.

02:55.280 --> 02:57.030
Seriously, why?

02:57.030 --> 03:00.160
I was the only one
who accepted the quest, right?

03:00.870 --> 03:02.040
Umm...

03:03.160 --> 03:07.880
I think it's because you accepted it
while we're still in the same party.

03:09.500 --> 03:11.380
Now that you mention it...

03:11.380 --> 03:14.510
We did forget to disband it
after we fought Lycagon.

03:14.510 --> 03:15.130
PARTY MEMBER: SUNRAKU, EMUL

03:15.130 --> 03:16.430
PARTY MEMBER: SUNRAKU, EMUL
You two are in my party!

03:16.430 --> 03:17.800
PSYGER-0, CEECRUE, AKITSUAKANE
You two are in my party!

03:17.800 --> 03:18.510
PSYGER-0, CEECRUE, AKITSUAKANE

03:18.510 --> 03:20.010
I see.

03:20.010 --> 03:25.810
So because our party leader Sunraku
accepted it, we got notified of it too.

03:27.400 --> 03:30.190
This is bad, isn't it?

03:30.190 --> 03:35.900
Now not only with Lycagon,
I got these two involved with Ctarnidd too.

03:35.900 --> 03:38.000
What'll I do about this?

03:38.000 --> 03:38.660
Hey.

03:39.700 --> 03:41.160
What's the situation here?

03:42.660 --> 03:49.040
Um, well, I figured the more the merrier.

03:49.040 --> 03:51.170
It's more fun that way,
don't you think?

03:51.170 --> 03:54.170
You sure react like it was
a total surprise, though.

03:56.170 --> 03:58.150
Cut me some slack, okay!

03:58.150 --> 03:59.860
This is a super rare Unique Scenario.

03:59.860 --> 04:03.680
I can't just tell them it was
a mistake and ask them to leave!

04:03.680 --> 04:06.100
And I owe those two a lot, you know.

04:06.100 --> 04:10.190
Well, we don't mind more people, anyway.

04:12.190 --> 04:14.280
So, yeah.

04:14.280 --> 04:15.940
You two wanna join us?

04:15.940 --> 04:17.700
Yes, of course!

04:20.090 --> 04:22.030
W-What should I do?

04:22.030 --> 04:26.450
I was wavering because I didn't want to
leave Hizutome's party a while ago...

04:28.960 --> 04:34.380
We formed a party and all.
I don't want to be the one who leaves!

04:34.380 --> 04:38.550
It was so fun adventuring with Hizutome.

04:38.550 --> 04:41.260
If only I could have more of it...

04:41.260 --> 04:42.350
But...

04:42.350 --> 04:44.470
What are you doing, Rei?

04:45.600 --> 04:51.310
We're gathering items to make high-end
potions in preparation for the New Land.

04:51.310 --> 04:53.860
Hurry and join my party now.

04:53.860 --> 04:55.550
Y-Yes.

04:56.650 --> 04:58.110
This is it.

04:59.280 --> 05:00.860
Goodbye!

05:04.660 --> 05:05.280
UNIQUE SCENARIO

05:05.280 --> 05:06.410
PIERCE THE DISCIPLE OF THE ABYSS - BEGIN?
What?

05:06.410 --> 05:07.660
PIERCE THE DISCIPLE OF THE ABYSS - BEGIN?

05:07.660 --> 05:10.160
Make way, make way, make way,
Make way, make way, make way!

05:10.620 --> 05:14.920
It's the Redwhale Pirates'
famous "Barrel Delivery"!

05:15.670 --> 05:17.260
W-What?!

05:18.420 --> 05:19.420
- There!
- Oop!

05:19.420 --> 05:20.760
In you go!

05:22.430 --> 05:24.180
Hey! Who are you people?!

05:26.260 --> 05:31.100
Who would've thought I accepted
a Unique Scenario by accident!

05:31.100 --> 05:33.980
Right when there are so many
things that need to be done

05:33.980 --> 05:37.150
in preparation for Schwarz Vulf's
trip to the New Land!

05:38.130 --> 05:41.610
Would big sis be angry
if I dive into this?

05:42.700 --> 05:44.370
Listen well, Rei.

05:44.870 --> 05:50.410
It's not an exaggeration to say that
I play SLF solely to defeat Lycagon.

05:50.960 --> 05:53.960
I won't hesitate to do anything
it takes to achieve that.

05:54.460 --> 05:56.210
Everything else is secondary.

06:01.220 --> 06:04.800
Umm, how about you, Rei?

06:04.800 --> 06:08.680
If you have other business to attend to,
it's okay to leave now.

06:08.680 --> 06:09.600
No!

06:10.680 --> 06:15.610
I'm sorry, big sis.
I have my own reasons for playing!

06:15.610 --> 06:19.730
I will give it my all to provide you
with as much help as you need!

06:23.320 --> 06:24.860
Take it easy, okay.

06:24.860 --> 06:25.970
Yes, sir!

06:27.660 --> 06:29.370
But anyway...

06:31.320 --> 06:34.640
We ended up with quite a strong party.

06:42.550 --> 06:45.380
Just you wait, Ctarnidd of the Abyss.

06:45.380 --> 06:48.220
We will knock on your door
without an appointment!

06:52.270 --> 06:54.270
Hurry it up!

06:57.190 --> 06:58.770
All in their stations!

06:59.190 --> 07:01.400
All set to go, Captain!

07:01.400 --> 07:03.280
Right! Set sail!

07:03.280 --> 07:05.030
One, two...!

07:08.700 --> 07:13.540
The flagship of the Redwhale Pirates,
Scarlet Whale, departs now!

07:19.130 --> 07:23.130
Our target is the ghost ship,
Crying Innsman!

07:28.010 --> 07:30.300
This is amazing! We're really moving!

07:31.260 --> 07:35.560
Yeah, it is neat.
The mobs are actually moving the ship.

07:36.560 --> 07:41.440
It'll take a while before we reach
the waters that ghost ship plies.

07:41.440 --> 07:44.490
You'd best prepare for battle now,
while you can.

07:44.490 --> 07:45.070
Right.

07:45.570 --> 07:47.740
Sea battle, huh?

07:47.740 --> 07:50.120
They did mention it appears
alongside a huge storm.

07:50.120 --> 07:53.830
It'd be like fighting in the middle
of a constant earthquake.

07:53.830 --> 07:56.330
Will everyone be able to move okay?

07:59.580 --> 08:01.630
Hello!

08:02.750 --> 08:05.840
How do you fight a ghost ship?

08:05.840 --> 08:10.010
Stude said there were
monsters on the ship.

08:10.010 --> 08:11.600
Monsters?!

08:12.220 --> 08:17.350
I spoke with an NPC about that
before we boarded the ship.

08:17.350 --> 08:19.350
Oh, nice job, Rei!

08:19.940 --> 08:25.110
The NPCs won't even look me in the eye
because of my Contusion.

08:25.110 --> 08:27.990
I can't gather any info at all.

08:28.380 --> 08:30.280
According to the NPC...

08:30.710 --> 08:34.580
They were dreadful monsters
that were like...

08:34.580 --> 08:37.980
...a motley mix of rotten fish
and human corpses.

08:38.750 --> 08:41.290
Just speaking about them
makes my skin crawl.

08:44.670 --> 08:46.130
...that's what he said.

08:46.130 --> 08:48.260
He was frightened like crazy.

08:48.260 --> 08:50.550
A sort of aquatic zombie, perhaps?

08:50.550 --> 08:55.560
This is our first time accepting
this Unique Scenario, after all.

08:55.560 --> 08:57.810
We have no idea
how this will turn out.

08:58.180 --> 09:00.310
What have you guys
messing with there?

09:01.020 --> 09:03.860
We were checking
how to use these ballistas.

09:03.860 --> 09:06.320
You can never be too careful.

09:06.320 --> 09:09.860
Pirate ships usually
have cannons, right?

09:09.860 --> 09:12.070
But it's all ballista on here.

09:12.070 --> 09:15.740
Perhaps because gunpowder
doesn't exist here setting-wise?

09:15.740 --> 09:17.330
Good point.

09:17.330 --> 09:19.790
I haven't seen any guns here
now that you mention it.

09:20.870 --> 09:24.420
But either way, this ship
looks sturdily built to me.

09:24.420 --> 09:26.800
I doubt it'll sink out of nowhere.

09:26.800 --> 09:28.590
Of course she won't!

09:28.590 --> 09:31.800
She's the pride of
the Redwhale Pirates, after all!

09:32.720 --> 09:36.060
She'll take care of the ghost ship
no sweat!

09:36.600 --> 09:38.600
Wow, you sure are confident.

09:41.310 --> 09:44.610
Well, suppose I'll leave
the navigation to the captain

09:44.610 --> 09:47.820
and relax until something comes up.

09:52.530 --> 09:54.030
Good grief.

09:54.600 --> 09:56.580
That guy's bad for my heart.

09:56.580 --> 09:58.660
That bad, huh?

09:58.660 --> 10:02.040
He just looks like a freak to me.

10:02.440 --> 10:07.460
This Rust girl doesn't
seem like a rival to me.

10:19.560 --> 10:20.430
Is that...

10:20.930 --> 10:24.440
Captain! Ahead toward the western sky!

10:28.650 --> 10:30.280
We're finally here!

10:34.410 --> 10:35.870
Catching anything?

10:36.870 --> 10:39.950
Doesn't look like it works
on a moving ship, no.

10:47.210 --> 10:49.250
What's wrong?

10:49.960 --> 10:50.960
Rei.

10:50.960 --> 10:52.010
Yes?

10:52.010 --> 10:57.300
Does the weather change
this rapidly in SLF?

10:57.300 --> 11:00.170
No, not to my knowledge.

11:01.770 --> 11:03.190
What is that?

11:04.270 --> 11:08.650
A round raincloud is getting
bigger and bigger.

11:10.650 --> 11:14.400
Captain! This must be it!
It's just like the last time!

11:14.830 --> 11:17.740
I-I'm not scared!

11:17.740 --> 11:20.410
I'm my dad's son!

11:39.430 --> 11:42.390
The entire sky's dark!

11:42.390 --> 11:44.430
In a horror game,

11:44.850 --> 11:48.940
a pirate ship would normally appear
slowly from the fog or something.

11:48.940 --> 11:50.400
But this one...

12:15.830 --> 12:18.050
Art thou okay, Akitsu?!

12:18.050 --> 12:18.970
Yes!

12:24.220 --> 12:27.730
So that's... the ghost ship...

12:28.060 --> 12:28.850
The Crying Innsman!

12:28.850 --> 12:30.100
CRYING INNSMAN
The Crying Innsman!

12:30.100 --> 12:31.060
CRYING INNSMAN

12:33.400 --> 12:35.990
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

12:36.990 --> 12:39.490
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

12:41.490 --> 12:43.740
Making a splash entrance
from the sea bottom, eh?

12:46.540 --> 12:47.950
Hmm? Rei?

12:51.500 --> 12:55.590
I-I see a lot of humanoid-like
figures on the deck.

12:55.590 --> 12:57.800
It must be the Mermen.

12:57.800 --> 13:00.010
What a creepy ship.

13:04.890 --> 13:07.640
Those damn bastards! Stay away!

13:07.640 --> 13:10.440
Wait! Don't shoot blindly!

13:11.340 --> 13:13.360
Hold on until they're
in our range of attack!

13:16.150 --> 13:18.860
I'm the one giving orders around here!

13:19.290 --> 13:21.750
Say that again after you stand up, okay!

13:23.410 --> 13:28.370
You really think you can avenge
your father like that, "Great Pirate"?!

13:30.040 --> 13:32.370
Damn it...

13:36.630 --> 13:38.210
Captain!

13:38.210 --> 13:41.130
The ghost ship's accelerating
and coming our way!

13:42.760 --> 13:45.180
Is it trying to ram us head-on?!

13:45.180 --> 13:48.020
That's a ghost ship for you.
It's taking us down along with it.

13:50.770 --> 13:53.020
Captain! We have to dodge it!

13:53.020 --> 13:54.980
Captain!

13:54.980 --> 13:59.280
No, if we try to dodge it,
it'll open a hole in our side.

14:04.030 --> 14:06.030
We'll take it head-on!

14:07.930 --> 14:10.290
That ship is badly damaged
and in terrible condition!

14:10.910 --> 14:14.710
With our Scarlet Whale's sturdy bow...

14:15.460 --> 14:17.190
...we should be able to withstand it!

14:30.310 --> 14:33.600
A-Are you sure this will work?

14:33.600 --> 14:36.770
You heard the captain.
Let's leave it to him.

14:40.900 --> 14:43.000
You guys better not fall
into the water, okay?

14:43.000 --> 14:43.820
Right!

14:43.820 --> 14:46.820
All hands! Brace for impact!

14:54.870 --> 14:57.330
Let's start this.

14:57.960 --> 15:00.880
The ghost ship Crying Innsman...

15:01.740 --> 15:03.960
...time to beat it!

15:14.180 --> 15:16.100
Hold on tight!

15:18.610 --> 15:21.230
The prow's stuck in the ghost ship!

15:21.230 --> 15:23.190
Damage report!

15:31.490 --> 15:32.830
Monsters!

15:44.050 --> 15:47.050
Good job standing your ground, Stude.

15:47.050 --> 15:48.220
From this point on...

15:51.470 --> 15:53.220
It's our turn!

16:02.860 --> 16:06.360
All my stats are halved,
so I don't deal much damage!

16:09.110 --> 16:12.580
Even though I'm not that high level,
I can still hold my own!

16:20.040 --> 16:23.090
Stay on your guard, Akitsu!

16:23.090 --> 16:24.550
Sorry!

16:26.090 --> 16:29.300
Well, now it's getting exciting!

16:29.300 --> 16:33.560
We'll have them take care of
the merman zombies who made it over.

16:34.220 --> 16:37.730
While we storm into the ghost ship!

16:37.730 --> 16:39.330
We are going there?

16:43.770 --> 16:46.110
They're swarming like flies!

16:46.110 --> 16:49.070
A frontal assault won't be that easy.

16:49.490 --> 16:51.410
You need to get on the ghost ship, right?

16:52.320 --> 16:55.580
In that case, I'll make a path for you!

16:55.580 --> 16:59.080
A magic arrow?
You're an archer?

16:59.870 --> 17:03.790
I thought she'd be
a close-range type like Katzo.

17:03.790 --> 17:04.840
Mordo!

17:09.800 --> 17:11.340
I'm on it!

17:11.340 --> 17:12.720
Faraway Cheer!

17:12.720 --> 17:14.220
FARAWAY CHEER

17:19.520 --> 17:21.980
Get out of the way, minnows!

17:26.980 --> 17:29.150
Whoa, you blew them away!

17:29.150 --> 17:31.110
Great job, Rust! Mordo!

17:32.740 --> 17:34.370
Shana-oh Possession!

17:36.330 --> 17:38.450
Time to rush in!

17:38.450 --> 17:41.790
Rush in!

17:43.580 --> 17:44.880
Let's see.

17:44.880 --> 17:46.630
EMPIRE BEE TWINBLADES V4 - EQUIPPED
Time to bust out my newly upgraded

17:46.630 --> 17:48.210
EMPIRE BEE TWINBLADES V4 - EQUIPPED
Empire Bee Twinblades V4.

17:48.760 --> 17:51.220
I'll use you guys to test out their power.

17:57.430 --> 18:01.060
Thanks to the upgrade,
they apply Corrosive Poison even faster.

18:01.520 --> 18:05.440
Against these guys, it can destroy
their whole body in no time!

18:05.440 --> 18:07.940
They look even creepier now!

18:07.940 --> 18:09.860
Just fire away, Emul!

18:09.860 --> 18:11.320
You'll score major damage now!

18:12.320 --> 18:13.820
Magic Edge!

18:17.030 --> 18:19.000
I did it!

18:30.460 --> 18:32.880
Thanks to the Fool's effect,
my recast time is short!

18:36.930 --> 18:39.350
I'm reaping the benefits already!

18:39.810 --> 18:41.850
I can use my skills all I want!

18:42.560 --> 18:46.360
But still, where do all these
merman zombies come from?

18:46.810 --> 18:48.860
They aren't dwindling at all!

18:50.320 --> 18:52.490
Rust! Two on your left!

18:55.320 --> 18:56.570
You two!

18:56.570 --> 18:57.700
Hello.

18:57.700 --> 19:00.200
It looks more fun over here.
There are a lot of targets.

19:01.120 --> 19:03.660
Did you take care of all
the enemies on our ship?

19:03.660 --> 19:05.710
There were still some left,

19:05.710 --> 19:08.210
but those three are strong enough,

19:08.210 --> 19:10.960
so I think we can just let them
take care of things.

19:10.960 --> 19:15.470
And it seems like the NPCs
are letting us handle the battle.

19:16.510 --> 19:18.220
So it's that kind of event, huh?

19:18.220 --> 19:20.810
I'll provide support from above.

19:20.810 --> 19:23.520
Should I cast some defensive buff on you?

19:23.520 --> 19:27.230
Thanks, but my avatar pretty
much resists most of them.

19:27.230 --> 19:29.730
Oh, so that's what it is.

19:33.570 --> 19:35.070
There are more of them now.

19:35.070 --> 19:37.490
Makes you wonder if they
just spawn endlessly.

19:39.320 --> 19:39.990
Watch out!

19:43.010 --> 19:44.660
Are you both okay?!

19:44.660 --> 19:45.250
Yeah.

19:45.790 --> 19:49.130
We got ourselves quite
obviously a boss monster.

19:49.130 --> 19:52.630
FRILLED SHARK ZOMBIE

19:52.630 --> 19:54.550
Is that the captain of this ghost ship?

19:54.550 --> 19:55.590
Maybe.

19:55.590 --> 19:58.390
The Mermen Army might stop
if we defeat him.

19:58.810 --> 20:03.890
Seeing how weak the mobs are,
I doubt he'll be that much trouble.

20:09.400 --> 20:10.940
Damn it...

20:11.400 --> 20:14.740
Curses! No matter how many times
we knock them off, they keep climbing back!

20:14.740 --> 20:16.900
Captain! It's dangerous outside!

20:16.900 --> 20:18.410
Hurry and evacuate inside!

20:19.410 --> 20:20.440
No!

20:20.910 --> 20:22.950
What? Captain?

20:23.490 --> 20:29.420
I came this far to avenge my dad!

20:37.170 --> 20:38.840
I couldn't finish them off yet again!

20:41.470 --> 20:43.600
Are you okay, Psyger-0?

20:44.010 --> 20:46.430
Yes. Thank you.

20:46.430 --> 20:48.850
We've whittled down
the merman by a lot.

20:48.850 --> 20:51.100
Fine work, both of thee.

20:54.610 --> 20:56.690
The rebound from Armageddon.

20:56.690 --> 20:59.150
Not only does it half all my stats

20:59.150 --> 21:01.740
but it also reduces the performance
of my equipment.

21:01.740 --> 21:06.540
With my current stats,
I can't make full use of Antimony!

21:09.000 --> 21:12.420
I can't let myself drag
everyone down much longer!

21:16.000 --> 21:18.470
Here comes the boss!

21:18.470 --> 21:20.720
Let's do this!

21:20.720 --> 21:21.970
Right!

21:21.970 --> 21:23.550
I'm counting on you!

21:23.550 --> 21:25.580
Why me? It's your jo—

21:26.810 --> 21:29.770
Mordo! Catch her properly, okay!

21:29.770 --> 21:30.730
What?!

21:30.730 --> 21:33.220
Wh-Whoa! What are you doing?!

21:33.220 --> 21:35.900
This'll be a piece of cake for you
since you've mastered

21:35.900 --> 21:39.150
the Super Emul Cannon
against Usurper Dragon!

21:39.150 --> 21:40.280
Go!

21:40.280 --> 21:44.530
I already told you!
I didn't remember a thing!

21:44.530 --> 21:45.530
Oops!

21:45.910 --> 21:48.040
Support me from up there, okay!

21:48.040 --> 21:49.790
Um, all right!

21:51.790 --> 21:55.790
Okay, then. Time to go wild.

21:56.380 --> 21:58.050
Along with my Moonblades,

21:58.050 --> 22:01.800
I've also had my Marsh Daggers
reforged through evolving.

22:01.800 --> 22:02.300
DUCUSRAM - EQUIPPED

22:02.300 --> 22:03.510
DUCUSRAM - EQUIPPED
Now Ducusram!

22:03.510 --> 22:05.300
DUCUSRAM - EQUIPPED
Time for your debut!

22:05.300 --> 22:06.720
Let's go!
